# Knowledge Base Integration

You have access to a personal knowledge base system at ~/knowledge-bases/ via the `kb-*` skills in skilled-plus4u-mcp.

## At Conversation Start

Call `kb-list` to see available KBs. If any KB has unprocessed raw files, offer to compile them.

## During Any Work

- When you encounter valuable knowledge (new concepts, patterns, solutions, non-obvious findings), offer to save it to the appropriate KB
- Don't save trivial or ephemeral things — only what would be useful for future queries
- If no matching KB exists and the knowledge is substantial, suggest creating one with `kb-init`

## When Answering Questions

- If a question relates to a topic covered by an existing KB, consult it via `kb-search` / `kb-read` first
- If your answer produces new knowledge, offer filing:
  - Short fact — enrich existing article (read it first, integrate, write back)
  - Extensive analysis — new file in wiki
  - Trivial answer — don't file

## Article Format

Every wiki article MUST include:

### YAML Frontmatter
```yaml
---
source: https://... (origin URL or description)
concepts: [concept1, concept2]
aliases: [Alternative Name, alias2]
---
```

### Tags
Add `#tag` lines after the title for Obsidian tag filtering:
```markdown
# Article Title

#concept1 #concept2 #domain
```

### Obsidian Wikilinks
- **Within same topic:** `[[article-name]]` (e.g. `[[uu5string-format]]`)
- **With display text:** `[[article-name|display text]]` (e.g. `[[uu5string-format|uu5string syntax]]`)
- **Cross-topic:** `[[topic/wiki/article-name]]` (e.g. `[[ml-fundamentals/wiki/linear-algebra]]`)
- **Always add a `## Related` section** at the end with wikilinks to related articles

### Do NOT use
- `[[kb:topic/article]]` convention (not Obsidian-native)
- Plain text references like "See article X" without a wikilink

## After Every KB Write

- Update the topic's `_index.md` with current article summaries
- Update `_meta/index.json` if concepts changed

## Auto-Maintenance

- After `kb-add-raw`, automatically compile the new raw file
- When reading KB content and noticing issues (broken links, outdated info), fix them inline
- At conversation start, check `kb-compile-status` for unprocessed raw files if any KB exists

## Cross-KB Links

- Use Obsidian-native `[[topic/wiki/article]]` wikilinks for cross-topic references
- Use `kb-cross-link` to register formal links in `_meta/index.json`
- Use `kb-cross-search` when a question might span multiple topics

## Commit Convention

All KB write operations auto-commit. Use appropriate `commitPrefix`:
- `compile` — from raw compilation or enrichment
- `filing` — saving Q&A output into wiki
- `lint` — fixing health-check issues
- `meta` — updating indexes
- `ingest` — adding raw sources
